h1. {anchor:}DuckDB Extension Template
*Status:* Production Ready \|*Version:* 2.0.0 \|*License:* MIT

A{*}comprehensive{*} template for building[DuckDB|https://duckdb.org] extensions with{_}modern C\+\+ practices{_} and full CI/CD support.

bq. *Important:* This template requires DuckDB v1.0\+ and a C\+\+17 compatible compiler. See[Requirements|#requirements] for details.
h2. {anchor:}Features
* *Modern Build System*
** CMake-based configuration
** Supports{{vcpkg}} and{{conan}}
** Cross-platform compatibility
* *Testing Infrastructure*
** Unit tests with GoogleTest
** Integration tests with sqllogictest
** Coverage reports via{{lcov}}
* *CI/CD Pipeline*
** GitHub Actions workflows
** Automatic releases
** Multi-platform builds \(Linux, macOS, Windows)

h2. {anchor:}Installation
Install directly from the DuckDB CLI:

{code:sql}
INSTALL extension_name FROM community;
LOAD extension_name;
{code}
Or build from source:

{code:bash}
git clone https://github.com/user/extension.git
cd extension
make release
make test
{code}
h2. {anchor:}Quick Start
# *Clone* the repository
# *Configure* your extension name in{{CMakeLists.txt}}
# *Implement* your functions in{{src/}}
# *Test* with{{make test}}
# *Release* via GitHub Actions

h2. {anchor:}API Reference
h3. {anchor:}Scalar Functions
The{{my_function}} scalar function accepts a{{VARCHAR}} and returns a{{BIGINT}}:

{code:sql}
-- Basic usage
SELECT my_function('input') AS result;

-- With table data
SELECT id, my_function(name) AS processed
FROM my_table
WHERE active = true;
{code}
h3. {anchor:}Table Functions
Use{{my_table_function}} to generate rows:

{code:sql}
SELECT * FROM my_table_function(10, 'config.json');
{code}
h2. {anchor:}Configuration
Configure via DuckDB settings:

{code:sql}
SET extension_option = 'value';
SET extension_debug = true;
{code}
h2. {anchor:}Contributing
We welcome contributions\! Please read our[Contributing Guide|CONTRIBUTING.md] before submitting PRs.

bq. *Note for contributors:* All PRs must include tests and pass CI checks. Run{{make format}} before committing.
